Package: misskappa
Type: Package
Title: Agreement Coefficients with Missing Ratings
Version: 3.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Jonas", "Moss", , "jonas.moss.statistics@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6876-6964"))
Description: Estimates chance-corrected agreement coefficients (Cohen's,
    Conger's, and Fleiss' kappa and the Brennan-Prediger coefficient; Conger
    (1980) <doi:10.1037/0033-2909.88.2.322>) for any number of raters, with
    nominal, linear, or quadratic weights, when some ratings are missing.
    Missing ratings are handled by inverse-probability weighting (Horvitz and
    Thompson (1952) <doi:10.1080/01621459.1952.10483446>) when they are
    missing completely at random, and by categorical or robust normal-theory
    full-information maximum likelihood when they are missing at random
    (Little and Rubin (2019) <doi:10.1002/9781119482260>). Every estimate
    comes with an influence-function standard error, giving confidence
    intervals and Wald tests that compare coefficients across groups, raters,
    or estimators. Also handles counts-format data, multirater g-wise
    agreement (Moss (2024) <doi:10.1007/s11336-023-09945-2>), and
    vector-valued ratings.
